    {
      "refs": [
        "init:i1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To start, you need to identify the requirements for your trip."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly defines the process initiation point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n3",
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If you choose \"Select one way\", you can proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional establishes the XOR split, the guard extracts the exact comparison value, and the action models the chosen path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n4",
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if you choose \"Select return\", you can also continue with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The alternative conditional provides the second guard value and its corresponding action step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, you will need to select the departure city and then the destination city."
      ],
      "justification": "'After that' indicates the parallel branches rejoin (converge) before executing the two sequential city-selection actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once you have chosen the destination city, you can proceed to select the class."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the class selection instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the class is selected, you can then choose your seat."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the seat selection instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After selecting your seat, you will be prompted to enter the type and number of passengers."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the passenger data entry instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once you have entered this information, you can continue to the flight selection."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the flight selection instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "end:e1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, once you have completed the flight selection, the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicitly states the process termination point."
    }
  ],
